  "title": "Mau Piailug",
  "summary": "Mau Piailug was a master navigator from Satawal in the Caroline Islands. In 1976 he guided the canoe Hōkūleʻa from Hawaiʻi to Tahiti without instruments, the first such voyage on that route in over 600 years. He later taught Hawaiian navigators and died on Satawal in 2010, aged 78.",
